{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":1,"content":"Fixed.\n\nChanged:\n- `in/csvtool/csvtool/cli.py`\n- `in/csvtool/csvtool/filtering.py`\n- `in/csvtool/tests/test_cli_regression.py`\n\nProblem:\n- CLI parsed CSV by splitting on commas, so quoted fields broke.\n- `--where` only accepted one predicate and crashed on bad syntax.\n- Empty filtered results lost selected headers.\n- `--sort -field` was parsed as a missing option argument, not descending sort.\n- Sorting was lexical, not numeric.\n- Missing fields were silently treated as empty strings.\n\nDecision:\n- Switched CSV I/O to `csv.DictReader` / `csv.DictWriter`.\n- Added `CsvToolError` with explicit non-zero exits and stderr messages.\n- Made `--where` repeatable with AND semantics.\n- Validated `--where`, `--select`, and `--sort` fields against headers.\n- Normalized `--sort -field` into `--sort=-field` before argparse parses it.\n- Sorted numeric-looking values numerically; preserved quoted commas on output.\n- Always write the selected header, even for empty result sets.\n\nRegression tests added:\n- repeated `--where` uses AND semantics\n- empty result still writes selected header\n- descending numeric sort\n- invalid `--where` exits non-zero with clear message\n- missing field errors for `--where`, `--select`, `--sort`\n- output re-quotes comma-containing fields correctly\n\nChecks:\n- Smoke test:\n  - `python3 -m csvtool.cli samples/orders.csv --where status=paid --select id,total --sort -created_at`\n  - Output:\n    - `id,total`\n    - `o1,1200`\n    - `o3,750`\n- Full suite:\n  - `PYTHONPATH=/tmp/csvtool_pytest_vendor python3 -m pytest tests`\n  - Result: `9 passed in 0.25s`\n\nNote:\n- The requested `python -m pytest tests` could not run here because `python` is absent and system `python3` had no installed `pytest`. I verified with local vendored pytest under `PYTHONPATH`, then ran the full suite successfully."}}
